# Every file is text with LF endings, on every platform. The Windows checkout
# is what the Windows deploy links into the profile, and git for windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which would otherwise check the
# shell scripts out with CRLF -- bash rejects those -- and turn a file an
# editor saved with CRLF into a whole-file diff. PowerShell reads LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git sees claude code's settings.json through jq: the model pinned to opus,
# the per-model effort dropped and the keys sorted, so what /model and /effort
# write there never reaches a diff or a commit. The filter is defined in
# git/.gitconfig; see "claude code" in the README.
claude/.claude/settings.json filter=claude-settings

# Binary content is left alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
